  "text": "The results of this study indicate that reducing DI and increasing serum vitamin D levels may help alleviate frailty in older people. This finding provides important implications for public health policy; that is, when formulating measures to prevent and intervene in aging faltering, diet quality should be considered comprehensively, and the health level of the older people should be improved by improving their diet habits. In the future, further prospective studies are needed to determine the exact relationship between DII and frailty.",
